From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: make the RK3576 completion poll period
 tunable

PC_DONE is read-only in INTERRUPT_MASK on RK3576, so it cannot be routed
to the GIC and the driver polls it on an hrtimer instead of taking a
completion interrupt.  The period is hardcoded at 1 ms, and because a
submit cannot complete faster than one poll, that period IS the
per-submit floor on this SoC: every cost table for this part is a
submit-count table because of it.

Make it a module parameter and drop the default to 500 us, which is the
shortest period that is correct.

The bound is not the poll rate.  PC_DONE means the program counter
finished, not that the DPU's write DMA has drained, and the driver both
tears down the IOMMU mapping and signals the fence as soon as it sees
PC_DONE.  A long period hides that behind its own detection lag.  Measured
on an H96 MAX M9 with the int8 matmul gate, one run per point [HW sweep]:

  poll period       1000us  500us  250us  150us
  shapes passing    43/43   43/43  40/43  37/43

The IOMMU half of that is fixed separately (see "keep the IOMMU domain
attached across jobs", which takes the stall timeouts and NPU DMA errors
to zero at every period in this table).  What remains below 500 us is the
fence being signalled before the writes are visible, and it needs about
250 us of settle to close -- which costs as much as the shorter period
saves.  Measured with an 8x64x32 int8 matmul, n=300, us/submit:

  1000us, no settle    1654
   500us, no settle    1084
   250us, 250us settle 1182
   150us, 250us settle 1036
   100us, 250us settle  988

So 500 us with no settle is both the correct default and within 5% of the
best any shorter period reaches.  It is worth 1.53x on this probe against
the stock 1 ms, and the parameter is kept so the period can still be swept
when the visibility race is understood well enough to shorten it further.

At 500 us the full RK3576 gate set is clean: int8 matmul 43/43 three runs
in a row, the same gate 43/43 through the DPU's 32-bit wide writer,
convolution 102/102, the convolution library 111 + 1 refused, the refusal
gate 9/9, the fp16 sweep's int8 control 2048/2048, and nothing in dmesg.

RK3588 takes a completion interrupt and does not poll at all, so it is
untouched.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index 135ffb2ed..99ceec54c 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -29,7 +29,21 @@
  */
 #define PC_INTERRUPT_MASK_RK3576_PC_DONE_0  0x10000000u
 #define PC_INTERRUPT_MASK_RK3576_PC_DONE_1  0x20000000u
-#define RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS  1000000LL  /* 1 ms */
+#define RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_US_DEFAULT  500u   /* 500 us */
+
+static unsigned int rocket_poll_interval_us = RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_US_DEFAULT;
+module_param_named(poll_interval_us, rocket_poll_interval_us, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(poll_interval_us,
+		 "RK3576 PC_DONE completion poll period, in microseconds (default 500)");
+
+static inline ktime_t rocket_poll_period(void)
+{
+	unsigned int us = READ_ONCE(rocket_poll_interval_us);
+
+	if (!us)
+		us = 1;
+	return ns_to_ktime((s64)us * NSEC_PER_USEC);
+}
 
 /*
  * PC_TASK_CON packs TASK_NUMBER in the low bits with the control bits directly
@@ -191,7 +205,7 @@ static void rocket_job_hw_submit(struct rocket_core *core, struct rocket_job *jo
 
 	if (core->soc->poll_completion) {
 		atomic_set(&core->poll_active, 1);
-		hrtimer_start(&core->poll_timer, ns_to_ktime(RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS),
+		hrtimer_start(&core->poll_timer, rocket_poll_period(),
 			      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
 	} else {
 		dev_dbg(core->dev, "Submitted regcmd at 0x%llx to core %d",
@@ -395,7 +409,7 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart rocket_poll_timer_fn(struct hrtimer *timer)
 		return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 	}
 
-	hrtimer_forward_now(timer, ns_to_ktime(RK3576_POLL_INTERVAL_NS));
+	hrtimer_forward_now(timer, rocket_poll_period());
 	return HRTIMER_RESTART;
 }
 
-- 
